### =====================================================================
### CAMPAIGNS  — proves CampaignController -> CampaignOrchestrator
###              -> CampaignService -> CampaignRepository
### =====================================================================

### 1. List campaigns (should be [] on a fresh start)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns
Accept: application/json

### 2. Create a campaign  (expect 201 Created + a JSON body with "id": 1)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Curse of Strahd",
  "description": "A gothic horror campaign set in Barovia.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "worldLore": "The land of Barovia is trapped in mists, ruled by the vampire Strahd von Zarovich."
}

### 3. List campaigns again (should now contain the campaign above)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get a single campaign by id
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2
Accept: application/json

### 5. Update the campaign (expect the new name in the response)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Curse of Strahd (Revised)",
  "description": "A gothic horror campaign set in Barovia.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "worldLore": "The mists have thickened. Strahd watches from Castle Ravenloft."
}

### 6. ERROR CASE: get a campaign that does not exist
###    Expect 404 + {"error": "Campaign 999 not found"}
###    This proves the GlobalExceptionHandler works.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/999
Accept: application/json


### =====================================================================
### SESSIONS — proves the nested Campaign -> Session relationship
### =====================================================================

### 7. Add a session to campaign 1 (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Into the Mists",
  "sessionNumber": 1,
  "date": "2026-08-06",
  "notes": "The party entered Barovia and met the Burgomaster.",
  "summary": "Session 1: arrival in Barovia."
}

### 8. Add a second session
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Village of Barovia",
  "sessionNumber": 2,
  "date": "2026-08-13",
  "notes": "The party explored the village and found Ireena.",
  "summary": "Session 2: meeting Ireena Kolyana."
}

### 9. List sessions for campaign 1 (should return both, ordered by sessionNumber)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/sessions
Accept: application/json

### 10. Get one session directly
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/sessions/1
Accept: application/json


### =====================================================================
### CHARACTERS — the party playing in a campaign.
###   Also the best proof the SERVICE layer works, because the response
###   contains CALCULATED values that were never sent.
### =====================================================================

### 11. Add a player character to campaign 1.
###     Note: we send raw ability scores only.
###     Expect the response to also contain calculated fields:
###       strength 16  -> abilityModifiers.strength  = +3
###       dexterity 14 -> initiative                 = +2
###       wisdom 12    -> passivePerception          = 11
###       level 5      -> proficiencyBonus           = 3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/characters
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aria the Bold",
  "playerName": "Jay",
  "characterClass": "Fighter",
  "race": "Human",
  "background": "Soldier",
  "level": 5,
  "strength": 16,
  "dexterity": 14,
  "constitution": 15,
  "intelligence": 10,
  "wisdom": 12,
  "charisma": 8,
  "maxHitPoints": 44,
  "armorClass": 17,
  "backstory": "A veteran of the border wars, searching for her missing brother."
}

### 12. Add a second party member
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/characters
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wren Nightwhisper",
  "playerName": "Sam",
  "characterClass": "Rogue",
  "race": "Half-Elf",
  "background": "Criminal",
  "level": 5,
  "strength": 8,
  "dexterity": 18,
  "constitution": 12,
  "intelligence": 14,
  "wisdom": 13,
  "charisma": 15,
  "maxHitPoints": 33,
  "armorClass": 15,
  "backstory": "Fled the thieves' guild of Waterdeep with a stolen ledger."
}

### 13. List the party of campaign 1 (both characters, ordered by name)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/characters
Accept: application/json

### 14. Get one character (with all calculated stats)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/characters/1
Accept: application/json

### 15. Update a character (e.g. level up + damage taken)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/characters/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aria the Bold",
  "playerName": "Jay",
  "characterClass": "Fighter",
  "race": "Human",
  "background": "Soldier",
  "level": 9,
  "strength": 18,
  "dexterity": 14,
  "constitution": 16,
  "intelligence": 10,
  "wisdom": 12,
  "charisma": 8,
  "maxHitPoints": 80,
  "currentHitPoints": 52,
  "armorClass": 18,
  "backstory": "A veteran of the border wars, now sworn to destroy Strahd.",
  "active": true
}

### 16. Campaign now reports characterCount = 2 and sessionCount = 2
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1
Accept: application/json

### 17. ERROR CASE: add a character to a campaign that does not exist
###     Expect 404 + {"error": "Campaign 999 not found"}
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/999/characters
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost"
}

### 18. Delete a character (expect 204 No Content)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/characters/2

### 19. List all characters across every campaign
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/characters
Accept: application/json


